/** @mainpage

atpg is a gate-level Automatic Test Pattern Generation tool for combinational
digital circuits, built on [slang](https://sv-lang.com) for its SystemVerilog
frontend.

It takes a hierarchical design built from SystemVerilog gate primitives,
flattens it into a gate-level netlist, derives the stuck-at fault list, and
produces a set of input vectors that detects those faults - together with the
response each vector should produce. The result can be written as an IEEE 1450
STIL program for a tester flow.

@section pipeline The pipeline

Each stage is a separate module, and each consumes the previous stage's output:

- @ref atpg::frontend flattens SystemVerilog into a gate netlist.
- @ref atpg::ir holds that netlist as a levelized graph.
- @ref atpg::sim evaluates it for one input vector.
- @ref atpg::fault enumerates and collapses the stuck-at fault list.
- @ref atpg::gen generates a test per fault class using a SAT-based miter
  construction, or proves the fault redundant.
- @ref atpg::fsim fault-simulates a pattern set bit-parallel to report coverage.
- @ref atpg::compact shrinks a pattern set to an irredundant subset with
  identical coverage.
- @ref atpg::stil renders the result as a STIL program.

@section features Features

- Fault collapsing by local equivalence and the checkpoint theorem.
- SAT-based test generation on OR-Tools CP-SAT, which proves redundancy rather
  than merely failing to find a test.
- A generate-and-drop loop that fault-simulates each pattern to skip the solver
  for faults it already covers.
- Bit-parallel fault simulation, 64 patterns per machine word, with each fault
  re-simulated only over its own fanout cone.
- Greedy pattern compaction producing an irredundant vector set.

@section guides Guides

- @ref user-guide - building the tool and running it.
- @ref developer-guide - how the modules fit together, and the conventions the
  code follows.

@section support Support and contributions

- Bug reports: [open an issue](https://github.com/jameshanlon/atpg/issues) on
  GitHub.
- Source: [github.com/jameshanlon/atpg](https://github.com/jameshanlon/atpg).

*/
